WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.622
Here’s how to run “The story behind me”.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:13.905
It’s the warm-up for the “Who are we?” conversation, and it works best when the team is new, or when people need to see each other as humans first.

00:00:13.955 --> 00:00:16.209
Plan four to five minutes per person.

00:00:16.259 --> 00:00:19.180
For a team of eight, that’s about forty minutes.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:25.229
Before the session, ask everyone to bring one photograph or object that says something important about them.

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:26.739
Not their biggest achievement.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:28.770
Just something that matters to them.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.973
A photo of a place, a gift, a tool, an old mug.

00:00:33.023 --> 00:00:34.749
Tell them it can be small.

00:00:34.799 --> 00:00:36.427
Start with your own story.

00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:37.186
Keep it short and real.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:44.027
When you go first, you show the level of openness, and you show that it’s fine to choose something simple.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.755
Then go round the circle.

00:00:45.805 --> 00:00:51.653
Each person shows their photo or object, tells the story behind it, and says why they chose it.

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:54.770
The listeners have one job: be curious.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.093
They can ask a question or two, like “What happened next?” or “What does it mean to you today?”

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:03.324
But they don’t analyse, interpret or give advice.

00:01:03.374 --> 00:01:06.441
This is not therapy, and it’s not a job interview.

00:01:06.491 --> 00:01:10.130
Keep time gently. Four to five minutes each is enough.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.484
If someone runs long, thank them warmly and move on.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.883
There’s nothing to fill in on the canvas for this one.

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:23.252
The result is something you can’t write down: people know a little more about each other, and that makes everything after it easier.

00:01:23.302 --> 00:01:27.683
Close with a short round: “What did you learn about someone today that surprised you?”

00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:31.396
And if you have time, move straight on to the personal user manual.

00:01:31.446 --> 00:01:34.352
The trust you just built makes it much more honest.

